# apps/automation (FastAPI + Claude agents). Copy to .env.
#
# [S5-01] Rewritten to match docs/security.md §9.1/§9.7 and api-contracts §8.8a. The previous
# sketch (2026-09-20, never used) named SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY; S7-03 ruled that the
# orchestrator must never be service_role, and §9.7 item 1 says plainly: if this file still
# names that key, the ruling was not carried through. It is gone.
#
# Also gone: SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_ANON_KEY. This process speaks to Postgres directly and
# never through PostgREST, so it needs no Supabase REST credentials at all (§9.1 left that
# question to whoever wrote the orchestrator's calls — this is the answer).

# The dedicated, non-BYPASSRLS `agent` Postgres role (migration 34). Direct connection, no
# PostgREST. The role's password is set out of band by S1/the owner at plan.md step C5 and is
# never committed. Never put a service-role key here.
AUTOMATION_DATABASE_URL=

# Scoped to this host, rotated and capped per docs/security.md §9.3. Owner action D3.
# Optional in development: with no key the Accounting agent still computes and writes its
# figures and records that the narrative was skipped.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# How many queued tasks one `run-once` pass claims. Not a ceiling — the spend ceilings live in
# `agents.config`, which this role may read and may not write.
AUTOMATION_POLL_LIMIT=5
